      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Motor City was originally conceived as part of the 2003 Dubailand entertainment complex, a $64.3 billion vision that would span 278 km².",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dubailand",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Dubailand project, including Motor City, was paused in 2008 after the financial crisis but restarted in 2013 with $55 billion raised.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dubailand",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Motor City sits within the Attractions & Experience World zone of Dubailand, one of six themed “worlds” planned for the complex.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Motor City’s development was overseen by Tatweer, a Dubai Holding subsidiary, before being taken over by Dubai Properties Group.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dubailand",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "By 2025, several Dubailand projects, including those in Motor City, were slated to open, marking a revival of the original vision.",
